# Development Workflow & Best Practices

## Scripts and Commands
The project includes comprehensive npm scripts in [package.json](mdc:package.json):

```bash
# Development
npm run dev              # Start development server
npm run dev:turbo        # Start with Turbopack (faster)

# Building and Production
npm run build            # Build for production
npm run start            # Start production server

# Code Quality
npm run lint             # Run ESLint
npm run format           # Format code with Prettier
npm run format:check     # Check formatting without changes
npm run type-check       # Run TypeScript type checking
npm run check-all        # Run all quality checks
npm run ci               # CI pipeline (lint + format + type-check + build)

# Maintenance
npm run clean            # Clean build artifacts
```

## Code Quality Standards

### Pre-commit Checks
Always run quality checks before committing:
```bash
npm run check-all
```

### ESLint Configuration
The project uses ESLint with Next.js and TypeScript rules from [eslint.config.mjs](mdc:eslint.config.mjs):
- Next.js core web vitals
- TypeScript strict mode
- Consistent code formatting

### Prettier Integration
Code formatting is handled by Prettier with consistent configuration:
- Automatic formatting on save
- Consistent quote styles
- Proper indentation

## Git Workflow

### Branch Naming
- `feature/description` - New features
- `fix/description` - Bug fixes
- `refactor/description` - Code refactoring
- `docs/description` - Documentation updates

### Commit Messages
Use conventional commit format:
```
feat: add new hero component with animations
fix: resolve button visibility in dark mode
docs: update README with setup instructions
refactor: improve animation performance
```

## Development Environment

### Node.js Version
- Minimum: Node.js 18.18.0
- Recommended: Latest LTS version
- Use `.nvmrc` or similar for version management

### IDE Configuration
Recommended VS Code extensions:
- TypeScript and JavaScript Language Features
- Tailwind CSS IntelliSense
- ESLint
- Prettier
- Auto Rename Tag
- Bracket Pair Colorizer

## Performance Optimization

### Build Optimization
- Use Next.js Image component for images
- Implement proper code splitting
- Optimize bundle size with dynamic imports
- Use React.memo for expensive components

### Runtime Performance
- Implement proper loading states
- Use Suspense for lazy loading
- Optimize animations with Framer Motion
- Monitor Core Web Vitals

## Testing Strategy

### Manual Testing Checklist
- [ ] Test all pages in both light and dark modes
- [ ] Verify animations work smoothly
- [ ] Check responsive design on mobile/tablet
- [ ] Test form validation and submission
- [ ] Verify accessibility with screen readers
- [ ] Test keyboard navigation

### Browser Testing
- Chrome (latest)
- Firefox (latest)
- Safari (latest)
- Edge (latest)

## Deployment

### Build Process
```bash
npm run ci  # Runs all checks and builds
```

### Environment Variables
- Set up proper environment variables for production
- Use Next.js built-in environment variable handling
- Never commit sensitive data

## Troubleshooting

### Common Issues
1. **Build Errors**: Run `npm run clean` then `npm run build`
2. **Type Errors**: Run `npm run type-check` for detailed errors
3. **Lint Errors**: Run `npm run lint` and fix issues
4. **Animation Issues**: Check Framer Motion version compatibility

### Performance Issues
- Use React DevTools Profiler
- Monitor bundle size with `npm run build`
- Check Core Web Vitals in production

## Documentation

### Code Documentation
- Use JSDoc comments for complex functions
- Document component props with TypeScript interfaces
- Include usage examples in component files

### README Updates
- Keep [README.md](mdc:README.md) updated with setup instructions
- Document any new dependencies or configuration changes
- Include troubleshooting section for common issues